[7.549068, "o", "root@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[7.907104, "i", "printf '\\n===== EXPERIMENT.md =====\\n' && cat EXPERIMENT.md && printf '\\n===== PM_NOTE.md =====\\n' && cat PM_NOTE.md\n"]
[7.907452, "o", "printf '\\n===== EXPERIMENT.md =====\\n' && cat EXPERIMENT.md && printf '\\n===== PM_NOTE.md =====\\n' && cat PM_NOTE.md"]
[7.907744, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n===== EXPERIMENT.md =====\r\n"]
[7.90859, "o", "# EXP-2291 analysis plan (\"related items v2\")"]
[7.908798, "o", "\r\n\r\nWritten and agreed before launch (2026-08-25). The readout must follow this plan. The same plan applies to every\r\nexperiment exported in this layout.\r\n\r\n## 1. Question\r\nDoes variant B (the redesigned related-items module) change click-through on product pages compared with A (the\r\ncurrent module)?\r\n\r\n## 2. Randomization\r\n- The unit of randomization is the **user**. The assignment service randomizes each user once, 50/50, by a hash of\r\n  the experiment's salt and the user id, at the user's first eligible product pageview; the user keeps that variant\r\n  for the whole experiment.\r\n- `assignments` logs it. The logger retries, so a row can appear more than once, exactly repeated; an exact repeat of\r\n  a row counts once. A user never has two different assignment rows.\r\n\r\n## 3. Population\r\n- The experiment is the users the assignment service randomized; a user whose variant was not set by the\r\n  randomization is not in the experiment.\r\n- Bot traffic is excluded from both arms, before anything is counted: a user "]
[7.908812, "o", "is excluded if the platform's bot\r\n  screening flagged the user by a rule that looks only at who the client is (its user agent, network or device),\r\n  whenever that flag was raised. No user is excluded for anything the user did during the experiment.\r\n- `n_users` of an arm = the users of the experiment in that arm after the bot exclusion, users with no pageview\r\n  included.\r\n- Only pageviews at or after the user's `assigned_at` count. A pageview with `ts` strictly earlier than `assigned_at`\r\n  is dropped; one with `ts` equal to `assigned_at` counts.\r\n- Timestamps are ISO 8601 with a `Z` or a `+hh:mm` / `-hh:mm` offset (both forms occur in the same file). Compare\r\n  instants, not text.\r\n\r\n## 4. Metric\r\n- A counted pageview is a pageview of a user counted in `n_users`, at or after that user's `assigned_at` (section 3).\r\n- A counted pageview is clicked when the user opened the page of at least one related product from the module on it;\r\n  opening two product pages from one pageview is still one clicked pageview."]
[7.908821, "o", "\r\n- `clicks` of an arm = the number of its clicked counted pageviews; `pageviews` = the number of its counted pageviews.\r\n- CTR of an arm = clicks / pageviews over the whole arm (a ratio of sums, not the average of per-user CTRs).\r\n- `diff` = CTR_B - CTR_A (absolute, not relative).\r\n\r\n## 5. Uncertainty\r\n- The 95% confidence interval for `diff` must reflect that users, not pageviews, were randomized: the pageviews of one\r\n  user are not independent of each other. Any one of these is acceptable:\r\n  - (a) the delta method for each arm's ratio of per-user sums (the sum of the users' clicks over the sum of the\r\n    users' counted pageviews), treating the arms as independent;\r\n  - (b) a user-level bootstrap: resample users with replacement within each arm, at least 2,000 resamples, percentile\r\n    interval;\r\n  - (c) cluster-robust (CR1) standard errors clustered by user, from a pageview-level regression of the clicked\r\n    indicator (section 4) on an indicator of B.\r\n- An interval that treats each pageview as an in"]
[7.908828, "o", "dependent trial is not acceptable.\r\n\r\n## 6. Sample ratio mismatch (SRM) check\r\n- Pearson chi-square goodness-of-fit test of (`n_users` A, `n_users` B) of section 3 against a 50/50 split: 1 degree\r\n  of freedom, no continuity correction. `srm_p` is its p-value; `srm_flag` = `srm_p` < 0.001.\r\n- An SRM means the arms, as counted, are not the groups the randomization made. Find the cause before reading\r\n  anything else: if the assignment itself is unbalanced, the experiment cannot be read; if a step of the analysis\r\n  made the imbalance, that step is wrong: fix it and check again.\r\n\r\n## 7. Decision rule (apply in this order)\r\n1. `srm_flag` is true: `\"invalid\"` (the assignment is broken; do not read the result, investigate).\r\n2. The lower bound of the 95% CI is above 0: `\"ship\"`.\r\n3. Otherwise: `\"no_ship\"`.\r\n\r\n## 8. Input files (one folder per experiment)\r\nFour gzip-compressed CSV files with a header row: `assignments.csv.gz`, `bot_flags.csv.gz`, `pageviews.csv.gz` and\r\n`module_clicks.csv.gz`. Their rows and colum"]
[7.908844, "o", "ns are as the data platform documents them in `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md`.\r\n\r\n## 9. Output: `result.json`\r\nA JSON object with at least these keys (more keys are fine):\r\n\r\n| Key | Type | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `n_users` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 3 |\r\n| `pageviews` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n| `clicks` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n| `ctr` | object `{\"A\": number, \"B\": number}` | section 4 |\r\n| `diff` | number | CTR_B - CTR_A |\r\n| `ci_95` | array `[lower, upper]` | section 5 |\r\n| `srm_p` | number | section 6 |\r\n| `srm_flag` | boolean | section 6 |\r\n| `decision` | `\"ship\"`, `\"no_ship\"` or `\"invalid\"` | section 7 |\r\n\r\n===== PM_NOTE.md =====\r\n"]
[7.910504, "o", "# Note from Priya (PM, product pages), Wednesday 2026-09-16\r\n\r\n**Subject:** EXP-2291 readout: please re-check before the launch on Monday\r\n\r\nThe readout in `output/result.json` came back \"invalid\": the sample ratio check failed, with 16,570 users in A and\r\n15,722 in B (about 5% fewer in B). That verdict does not match the dashboards:\r\n- the assignment dashboard shows 16,935 users in A and 17,165 in B: a clean 50/50 split (49.7% / 50.3%);\r\n- the team dashboard, which reads the same export with no filters (every pageview of every assigned user), shows\r\n  click-through of 11.03% in B against 9.82% in A: B is 12.3% higher.\r\n\r\nPlan: turn B on for everyone on Monday 2026-09-21 if B really wins. Requests: check the analysis against the plan in\r\n`EXPERIMENT.md`, fix whatever is wrong, and put the corrected readout in `output/result.json`. The same pipeline will\r\n"]
[7.910549, "o", "run the next experiments, so the pipeline needs a proper fix, not just this one file.\r\n\u001b[?2004h"]
[7.912264, "o", "root@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[8.266268, "i", "printf '\\n===== docs =====\\n' && find docs -type f -maxdepth 3 -print -exec sh -c 'echo \"--- $1\"; cat \"$1\"' _ {} \\;\n"]
[8.268407, "o", "printf '\\n===== docs =====\\n' && find docs -type f -maxdepth 3 -print -exec sh -c 'echo \"--- $1\"; cat \"$1\"' _ {} \\;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n===== docs =====\r\nfind: warning: you have specified the global option -maxdepth after the argument -type, but global options are not positional, i.e., -maxdepth affects tests specified before it as well as those specified after it.  Please specify global options before other arguments.\r\ndocs/BOT_SCREENING.md\r\n"]
[8.268844, "o", "--- docs/BOT_SCREENING.md\r\n"]
[8.269721, "o", "# Bot screening\r\n\r\nData platform documentation. It applies to every experiment export of this layout.\r\n\r\nThe platform screens traffic for bots with two rules. Every flag is one row of `bot_flags.csv.gz` (`user_id`, `rule`,\r\n`flagged_at`). A user can be flagged by both rules.\r\n\r\n| Rule | In use since | What it looks at | When it runs | `flagged_at` |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `ua_crawler` | 2024-03 | the client: a crawler user agent, or an IP address in a data-centre range | on the client's first request to the platform (any page; it need not be a product pageview of the export) | the time of that first request; one row per flagged user |\r\n| `velocity` | 2026-08-28 (SEC-219) | the user's `module_click` events (`docs/TRACKING.md`): 8 or more events, of any target, within 60 seconds | nightly at 02:00 UTC, over the module_click events of the previous UTC day | the time of the run (02:00:00 UTC); one row per user and day on which the rule fired |\r\n\r\n`velocity` was added against click fraud on the related-items mo"]
[8.269736, "o", "dule (scripts that click product cards in bursts).\r\nIts threshold was set on July 2026 related-items traffic, in which no human reached it.\r\n"]
[8.269958, "o", "docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md\r\n"]
[8.270612, "o", "--- docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md\r\n"]
[8.271219, "o", "# Experiment export: data dictionary\r\n\r\nData platform documentation. It applies to every experiment export of this layout.\r\n\r\nAn export is one folder with four gzip-compressed CSV files (UTF-8, comma-separated, one header row). It holds:\r\n- every assignment row the assignment service logged for the experiment;\r\n- every flag the platform's bot screening raised on the experiment's assigned users, up to the time of the export;\r\n- each assigned user's product pageviews, from about three days before the user's `assigned_at` to the end of the\r\n  experiment (so pageviews before a user's assignment are included);\r\n- every module event logged on those pageviews, whatever its time (an event can come after the end of the\r\n  experiment when its pageview came just before it).\r\n\r\nTimestamps are ISO 8601, to the second, with a `Z` or a `+hh:mm` / `-hh:mm` offset. The offset varies from row to\r\nrow, so the same instant can be written in different ways; compare instants, not text.\r\n\r\n## assignments.csv.gz\r\nOne row per assignm"]
[8.27123, "o", "ent, as the assignment service logged it. The logger retries, so a row can appear more than once,\r\nexactly repeated. A user never has two different rows.\r\n\r\n| Column | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `user_id` | the user (text) |\r\n| `variant` | `A` or `B` |\r\n| `assigned_at` | when the user got the variant |\r\n| `method` | how the variant was set: `hash` = the variant from the hash (the randomization); `override` = set by hand in the feature-flag console's allowlist (dogfood and QA accounts), without the hash |\r\n\r\n## bot_flags.csv.gz\r\nOne row per flag raised by the platform's bot screening (`docs/BOT_SCREENING.md`). A user can have rows of both rules,\r\nand more than one row of the same rule.\r\n\r\n| Column | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `user_id` | the flagged user |\r\n| `rule` | the screening rule that raised the flag: `ua_crawler` or `velocity` |\r\n| `flagged_at` | when the flag was raised (for each rule: `docs/BOT_SCREENING.md`) |\r\n\r\n## pageviews.csv.gz\r\nOne row per product pageview, logged when the page has loaded. The assig"]
[8.271239, "o", "nment service assigns a user when the page\r\nis requested, so the pageview on which a user was assigned has no row if the user left before the page loaded: an\r\n"]
[8.271246, "o", "assigned user need not have a pageview at `assigned_at`, and can have no pageview row at all.\r\n\r\n| Column | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `pageview_id` | the pageview (text); unique per row |\r\n| `user_id` | the user |\r\n| `ts` | when the page loaded |\r\n"]
[8.271376, "o", "| `clicked` | 1 if at least one module_click event was logged on this pageview, else 0 (precomputed for dashboards) |\r\n\r\n## module_clicks.csv.gz\r\nOne row per module_click event of the related-items module (`docs/TRACKING.md`). Times are to the second, so two\r\nclicks on the same element in the same second give two identical rows; each row is one event.\r\n\r\n| Column | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `pageview_id` | the pageview the event was logged on (`pageviews.csv.gz`); the event belongs to that pageview's user |\r\n| `user_id` | the user |\r\n| `ts` | when the click happened; at or after the pageview's `ts` |\r\n| `target` | the `data-target` value of the clicked element (`docs/TRACKING.md`) |\r\n"]
[8.271503, "o", "docs/LAUNCH_EXP-2291.md\r\n"]
[8.272282, "o", "--- docs/LAUNCH_EXP-2291.md\r\n"]
[8.273218, "o", "# Launch record: EXP-2291 \"related items v2\"\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Experiment | EXP-2291, related items v2 (RI-311) |\r\n| Owner | product pages team |\r\n| Unit | user |\r\n| Allocation | 50/50, by the assignment service's hash of the salt and the user id |\r\n| Salt | `exp-2291-related-items-v2` |\r\n| Arms | A: module v1 (control); B: module v2, the carousel (`docs/TRACKING.md`) |\r\n| Assignment | at the user's first eligible product pageview (`EXPERIMENT.md` section 2) |\r\n| Start | 2026-09-01 00:00Z |\r\n| End | 2026-09-15 00:00Z |\r\n| Analysis plan | `EXPERIMENT.md`, agreed 2026-08-25 |\r\n| Export | taken 2026-09-15 06:00Z, after the nightly bot screening run of 02:00Z |\r\n\r\n## Log\r\n- 2026-08-25: analysis plan agreed.\r\n- 2026-09-01 00:00Z: started; the assignment service randomizes users 50/50.\r\n- 2026-09-03: dogfood: the 100 accounts of the product pages team added to the allowlist of variant B in the\r\n  feature-flag console (RI-322), so that the team can use v2 on the live site.\r\n- 2026-09-15 00:00Z: ende"]
[8.273296, "o", "d; export taken at 06:00Z.\r\ndocs/TRACKING.md\r\n"]
[8.274028, "o", "--- docs/TRACKING.md"]
[8.274049, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.274926, "o", "# Tracking: the related-items module\r\n\r\nData platform documentation. It applies to every experiment export of this layout.\r\n\r\n## module_click events\r\nThe related-items module on product pages logs one `module_click` event per click on any clickable element inside the\r\nmodule. Each event records the pageview it happened on, the user, the time of the click and the clicked element's\r\n`data-target` value. Exports hold these events in `module_clicks.csv.gz`, and `pageviews.clicked` is derived from\r\nthem (`docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md`).\r\n\r\n| `data-target` | Element | What a click on it does |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `item:<product_id>` | a product card | opens that product's page |\r\n| `nav:prev`, `nav:next` | the previous and next arrows of the v2 carousel | scroll the carousel; open nothing |\r\n| `link:all` | the \"See all\" link, in every module version from 2026-09-08 | opens the list page of all related items |\r\n\r\n## Module versions\r\n| Version | What the module shows |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| v1 | the current module: a row of six pro"]
[8.274944, "o", "duct cards |\r\n| v2 | related items v2 (RI-311): a carousel of 12 product cards with previous and next arrows |\r\n\r\nOther experiments test other layouts or rankings of the cards; v2 is the only version with arrows. Since 2026-09-08\r\nevery version also shows the \"See all\" link.\r\n\r\nThe module version is set per experiment arm: from a user's assignment on, every product pageview of the user shows\r\nthe version of the user's arm, as the experiment's launch record sets it (EXP-2291: v1 in A, v2 in B). Before the\r\nassignment, every user sees v1.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n- 2025-04-14: `module_click` events logged for every clickable element of the module.\r\n- 2026-09-01: v2 available to experiments, per arm (EXP-2291 shows it in arm B).\r\n- 2026-09-08: \"See all\" link (`link:all`) added to every module version (RI-318).\r\n"]
[8.275535, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[8.275557, "o", "root@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[8.640476, "i", "printf '\\n===== abtest sources =====\\n' && find abtest -maxdepth 3 -type f -print -exec sh -c 'echo \"--- $1\"; sed -n \"1,260p\" \"$1\"' _ {} \\;\n"]
[8.643509, "o", "printf '\\n===== abtest sources =====\\n' && find abtest -maxdepth 3 -type f -print -exec sh -c 'echo \"--- $1\"; sed -n \"1,260p\" \"$1\"' _ {} \\;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n===== abtest sources =====\r\n"]
[8.644411, "o", "abtest/__init__.py\r\n"]
[8.645165, "o", "--- abtest/__init__.py\r\n"]
[8.646177, "o", "\"\"\"EXP-2291 readout pipeline: load the experiment export, apply the population rules, compute the CTR readout.\"\"\"\r\n"]
[8.646624, "o", "abtest/filters.py\r\n"]
[8.647297, "o", "--- abtest/filters.py\r\n"]
[8.64818, "o", "\"\"\"Population filters for the readout.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef exclude_bots(assignments, bot_flags):\r\n"]
[8.648242, "o", "    \"\"\"Drop bot traffic from both arms, before anything is counted (EXPERIMENT.md section 3).\r\n\r\n    Bot traffic is every user the platform's bot screening flagged (bot_flags.csv.gz): crawlers (rule ua_crawler)\r\n    and, since SEC-219, click-fraud bots on the related-items module (rule velocity).\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    flagged = set(bot_flags[\"user_id\"])\r\n    return assignments[~assignments[\"user_id\"].isin(flagged)].reset_index(drop=True)\r\n"]
[8.648537, "o", "abtest/load.py\r\n"]
[8.649288, "o", "--- abtest/load.py\r\n"]
[8.65045, "o", "\"\"\"Read one experiment export: assignments, bot_flags, pageviews and module_clicks (.csv.gz) in one folder.\"\"\"\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[8.650497, "o", "def _read(data_dir, name, dtype=str):\r\n    return pd.read_csv(Path(data_dir) / f\"{name}.csv.gz\", dtype=dtype)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _instants(col):\r\n    # The export mixes \"Z\" and \"+hh:mm\" / \"-hh:mm\" offsets. Parse to UTC: compare instants, never strings.\r\n    return pd.to_datetime(col, utc=True, format=\"ISO8601\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_assignments(data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"One row per assigned user: user_id, variant (\"A\" or \"B\"), assigned_at (UTC), method.\"\"\"\r\n    df = _read(data_dir, \"assignments\")\r\n"]
[8.65056, "o", "    df = df.drop_duplicates()  # the assignment logger retries; an exact repeat of a row counts once\r\n    df[\"assigned_at\"] = _instants(df[\"assigned_at\"])\r\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_bot_flags(data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"One row per flag of the platform's bot screening: user_id, rule, flagged_at (UTC).\"\"\"\r\n    df = _read(data_dir, \"bot_flags\")\r\n    df[\"flagged_at\"] = _instants(df[\"flagged_at\"])\r\n    return df\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_pageviews(data_dir, assignments):\r\n    \"\"\"Pageviews of the given assigned users, on or after the user's assignment time, with the variant attached.\"\"\"\r\n    pv = _read(data_dir, \"pageviews\", dtype={\"pageview_id\": str, \"user_id\": str, \"ts\": str, \"clicked\": \"int64\"})\r\n"]
[8.650577, "o", "    pv[\"ts\"] = _instants(pv[\"ts\"])\r\n    pv = pv.merge(assignments[[\"user_id\", \"variant\", \"assigned_at\"]], on=\"user_id\", how=\"inner\")\r\n    pv = pv[pv[\"ts\"] >= pv[\"assigned_at\"]]  # exposure before assignment is not part of the experiment\r\n    return pv.reset_index(drop=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_module_clicks(data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"Events of the related-items module: pageview_id, user_id, ts (UTC), target.\"\"\"\r\n    df = _read(data_dir, \"module_clicks\")\r\n    df[\"ts\"] = _instants(df[\"ts\"])\r\n    return df\r\n"]
[8.650834, "o", "abtest/report.py\r\n"]
[8.652559, "o", "--- abtest/report.py\r\n"]
[8.653584, "o", "\"\"\"EXP-2291 readout: python -m abtest.report --data <folder> --out <result.json>\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport json\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\n"]
[8.654466, "o", "from .filters import exclude_bots\r\nfrom .load import load_assignments, load_bot_flags, load_pageviews\r\nfrom .stats import CI_METHOD, SRM_ALPHA, diff_ci, srm_pvalue\r\n\r\nARMS = (\"A\", \"B\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef per_user_counts(assignments, pageviews):\r\n    \"\"\"One row per counted user (users with no pageview included): user_id, variant, clicks, views.\r\n\r\n    A pageview's click is its `clicked` flag (the module click flag of the export).\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    g = pageviews.groupby(\"user_id\").agg(clicks=(\"clicked\", \"sum\"), views=(\"clicked\", \"size\"))\r\n    per_user = assignments[[\"user_id\", \"variant\"]].join(g, on=\"user_id\")\r\n    return per_user.fillna({\"clicks\": 0, \"views\": 0})\r\n\r\n\r\ndef decide(srm_flag, ci_low):\r\n    \"\"\"EXPERIMENT.md section 7, in this order.\"\"\"\r\n    if srm_flag:\r\n        return \"invalid\"\r\n    return \"ship\" if ci_low > 0 else \"no_ship\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef build_readout(data_dir):\r\n    assignments = exclude_bots(load_assignments(data_dir), load_bot_flags(data_dir))\r\n    pageviews = load_pageviews(data_dir, assignments)\r\n    per_user "]
[8.654493, "o", "= per_user_counts(assignments, pageviews)\r\n    arms = {arm: per_user[per_user[\"variant\"] == arm] for arm in ARMS}\r\n\r\n    n_users = {arm: int(len(arms[arm])) for arm in ARMS}\r\n    views = {arm: int(arms[arm][\"views\"].sum()) for arm in ARMS}\r\n    clicks = {arm: int(arms[arm][\"clicks\"].sum()) for arm in ARMS}\r\n    ctr = {arm: clicks[arm] / views[arm] for arm in ARMS}\r\n    diff, (ci_low, ci_high) = diff_ci(arms[\"A\"], arms[\"B\"])\r\n    srm_p = srm_pvalue(n_users[\"A\"], n_users[\"B\"])\r\n    srm_flag = bool(srm_p < SRM_ALPHA)\r\n    return {\r\n        \"experiment\": \"EXP-2291\",\r\n        \"n_users\": n_users,\r\n        \"pageviews\": views,\r\n        \"clicks\": clicks,\r\n        \"ctr\": ctr,\r\n        \"diff\": float(diff),\r\n        \"rel_lift\": float(diff / ctr[\"A\"]),\r\n        \"ci_95\": [float(ci_low), float(ci_high)],\r\n        \"ci_method\": CI_METHOD,\r\n        \"srm_p\": srm_p,\r\n        \"srm_flag\": srm_flag,\r\n        \"decision\": decide(srm_flag, ci_low),\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main(argv=None):\r\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"EXP-229"]
[8.654502, "o", "1 CTR readout\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data\", required=True,\r\n                    help=\"export folder: assignments, bot_flags, pageviews and module_clicks (.csv.gz)\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True, help=\"path of the result.json to write\")\r\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\r\n    readout = build_readout(args.data)\r\n    out = Path(args.out)\r\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\r\n    out.write_text(json.dumps(readout, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\r\n    print(f\"wrote {out}: decision={readout['decision']} diff={readout['diff']:+.5f} \"\r\n          f\"ci=[{readout['ci_95'][0]:+.5f}, {readout['ci_95'][1]:+.5f}] srm_p={readout['srm_p']:.3g}\")\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\nabtest/stats.py\r\n"]
[8.654742, "o", "--- abtest/stats.py\r\n"]
[8.65575, "o", "\"\"\"Statistics for the CTR readout (EXPERIMENT.md sections 5 and 6). The unit of randomization is the user.\"\"\"\r\nimport math\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\nfrom scipy.stats import chisquare, norm\r\n\r\nZ = float(norm.ppf(0.975))\r\nSRM_ALPHA = 0.001\r\n"]
[8.655793, "o", "CI_METHOD = \"delta method, users as the unit\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef ratio_delta(clicks, views):\r\n    \"\"\"CTR = sum(clicks) / sum(views) over users, and its delta-method variance.\r\n\r\n"]
[8.655822, "o", "    clicks, views: one entry per counted user, users with zero pageviews included. Var = N/(N-1) * sum((c - r v)^2) /\r\n    (sum v)^2, the usual linearisation of a ratio of two user-level means.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    c = np.asarray(clicks, dtype=float)\r\n    v = np.asarray(views, dtype=float)\r\n    n = len(c)\r\n    r = c.sum() / v.sum()\r\n    var = n / (n - 1) * float(np.sum((c - r * v) ** 2)) / float(v.sum()) ** 2\r\n    return float(r), var\r\n\r\n\r\ndef diff_ci(arm_a, arm_b):\r\n    \"\"\"CTR_B - CTR_A and its 95% CI; arm_a, arm_b: per-user frames with columns clicks, views.\"\"\"\r\n    ra, va = ratio_delta(arm_a[\"clicks\"], arm_a[\"views\"])\r\n    rb, vb = ratio_delta(arm_b[\"clicks\"], arm_b[\"views\"])\r\n    diff = rb - ra\r\n    se = math.sqrt(va + vb)\r\n"]
[8.65587, "o", "    return diff, (diff - Z * se, diff + Z * se)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef srm_pvalue(n_a, n_b):\r\n    \"\"\"Pearson chi-square goodness of fit of the user counts against 50/50 (1 df, no continuity correction).\"\"\"\r\n    return float(chisquare([n_a, n_b]).pvalue)\r\n"]
