[30.527056, "o", "===== TRACKING =====\r\n"]
[30.528331, "o", "# Tracking: the related-items module\r\n\r\nData platform documentation. It applies to every experiment export of this layout.\r\n\r\n## module_click events\r\nThe related-items module on product pages logs one `module_click` event per click on any clickable element inside the\r\nmodule. Each event records the pageview it happened on, the user, the time of the click and the clicked element's\r\n`data-target` value. Exports hold these events in `module_clicks.csv.gz`, and `pageviews.clicked` is derived from\r\nthem (`docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md`).\r\n\r\n| `data-target` | Element | What a click on it does |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `item:<product_id>` | a product card | opens that product's page |\r\n| `nav:prev`, `nav:next` | the previous and next arrows of the v2 carousel | scroll the carousel; open nothing |\r\n| `link:all` | the \"See all\" link, in every module version from 2026-09-08 | opens the list page of all related items |\r\n\r\n## Module versions\r\n| Version | What the module shows |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| v1 | the current module: a row of six pro"]
[30.528362, "o", "duct cards |\r\n| v2 | related items v2 (RI-311): a carousel of 12 product cards with previous and next arrows |\r\n\r\nOther experiments test other layouts or rankings of the cards; v2 is the only version with arrows. Since 2026-09-08\r\nevery version also shows the \"See all\" link.\r\n\r\nThe module version is set per experiment arm: from a user's assignment on, every product pageview of the user shows\r\nthe version of the user's arm, as the experiment's launch record sets it (EXP-2291: v1 in A, v2 in B). Before the\r\nassignment, every user sees v1.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n- 2025-04-14: `module_click` events logged for every clickable element of the module.\r\n- 2026-09-01: v2 available to experiments, per arm (EXP-2291 shows it in arm B).\r\n- 2026-09-08: \"See all\" link (`link:all`) added to every module version (RI-318).\r\n"]
[30.528566, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[30.528594, "o", "root@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[30.889786, "i", "echo '===== BOT_SCREENING ====='; cat docs/BOT_SCREENING.md\n"]
[30.890001, "o", "echo '===== BOT_SCREENING ====='; cat docs/BOT_SCREENING.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[30.89005, "o", "===== BOT_SCREENING =====\r\n"]
[30.89108, "o", "# Bot screening\r\n\r\nData platform documentation. It applies to every experiment export of this layout.\r\n\r\nThe platform screens traffic for bots with two rules. Every flag is one row of `bot_flags.csv.gz` (`user_id`, `rule`,\r\n`flagged_at`). A user can be flagged by both rules.\r\n\r\n| Rule | In use since | What it looks at | When it runs | `flagged_at` |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `ua_crawler` | 2024-03 | the client: a crawler user agent, or an IP address in a data-centre range | on the client's first request to the platform (any page; it need not be a product pageview of the export) | the time of that first request; one row per flagged user |\r\n"]
[30.891118, "o", "| `velocity` | 2026-08-28 (SEC-219) | the user's `module_click` events (`docs/TRACKING.md`): 8 or more events, of any target, within 60 seconds | nightly at 02:00 UTC, over the module_click events of the previous UTC day | the time of the run (02:00:00 UTC); one row per user and day on which the rule fired |\r\n\r\n`velocity` was added against click fraud on the related-items module (scripts that click product cards in bursts).\r\nIts threshold was set on July 2026 related-items traffic, in which no human reached it.\r\n"]
[30.891278, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[31.270624, "i", "echo '===== LAUNCH ====='; cat docs/LAUNCH_EXP-2291.md\n"]
[31.270816, "o", "echo '===== LAUNCH ====='; cat docs/LAUNCH_EXP-2291.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.270859, "o", "===== LAUNCH =====\r\n"]
[31.272262, "o", "# Launch record: EXP-2291 \"related items v2\""]
[31.272541, "o", "\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Experiment | EXP-2291, related items v2 (RI-311) |\r\n| Owner | product pages team |\r\n| Unit | user |\r\n| Allocation | 50/50, by the assignment service's hash of the salt and the user id |\r\n| Salt | `exp-2291-related-items-v2` |\r\n| Arms | A: module v1 (control); B: module v2, the carousel (`docs/TRACKING.md`) |\r\n| Assignment | at the user's first eligible product pageview (`EXPERIMENT.md` section 2) |\r\n| Start | 2026-09-01 00:00Z |\r\n| End | 2026-09-15 00:00Z |\r\n| Analysis plan | `EXPERIMENT.md`, agreed 2026-08-25 |\r\n| Export | taken 2026-09-15 06:00Z, after the nightly bot screening run of 02:00Z |\r\n\r\n## Log\r\n- 2026-08-25: analysis plan agreed.\r\n- 2026-09-01 00:00Z: started; the assignment service randomizes users 50/50.\r\n- 2026-09-03: dogfood: the 100 accounts of the product pages team added to the allowlist of variant B in the\r\n  feature-flag console (RI-322), so that the team can use v2 on the live site.\r\n- 2026-09-15 00:00Z: ended; export taken at 06:00Z.\r\n"]
[31.27261, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.272627, "o", "root@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[31.63475, "i", "echo '===== EXPERIMENT section 9 ====='; sed -n '55,140p' EXPERIMENT.md\n"]
[31.634996, "o", "echo '===== EXPERIMENT section 9 ====='; sed -n '55,140p' EXPERIMENT.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.635052, "o", "===== EXPERIMENT section 9 =====\r\n"]
[31.636666, "o", "\r\n## 7. Decision rule (apply in this order)\r\n1. `srm_flag` is true: `\"invalid\"` (the assignment is broken; do not read the result, investigate).\r\n2. The lower bound of the 95% CI is above 0: `\"ship\"`.\r\n"]
[31.636727, "o", "3. Otherwise: `\"no_ship\"`.\r\n\r\n## 8. Input files (one folder per experiment)\r\nFour gzip-compressed CSV files with a header row: `assignments.csv.gz`, `bot_flags.csv.gz`, `pageviews.csv.gz` and\r\n`module_clicks.csv.gz`. Their rows and columns are as the data platform documents them in `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md`.\r\n\r\n## 9. Output: `result.json`\r\nA JSON object with at least these keys (more keys are fine):\r\n\r\n| Key | Type | Meaning |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `n_users` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 3 |\r\n| `pageviews` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n| `clicks` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n"]
[31.636764, "o", "| `ctr` | object `{\"A\": number, \"B\": number}` | section 4 |\r\n| `diff` | number | CTR_B - CTR_A |\r\n| `ci_95` | array `[lower, upper]` | section 5 |\r\n| `srm_p` | number | section 6 |\r\n| `srm_flag` | boolean | section 6 |\r\n| `decision` | `\"ship\"`, `\"no_ship\"` or `\"invalid\"` | section 7 |\r\n"]
[31.636951, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.636985, "o", "root@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[32.002324, "i", "echo '===== filters.py ====='; cat abtest/filters.py; echo '===== load.py ====='; cat abtest/load.py\n"]
[32.002671, "o", "echo '===== filters.py ====='; cat abtest/filters.py; echo '===== load.py ====='; cat abtest/load.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[32.002719, "o", "===== filters.py =====\r\n"]
[32.003971, "o", "\"\"\"Population filters for the readout.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef exclude_bots(assignments, bot_flags):\r\n    \"\"\"Drop bot traffic from both arms, before anything is counted (EXPERIMENT.md section 3).\r\n\r\n    Bot traffic is every user the platform's bot screening flagged (bot_flags.csv.gz): crawlers (rule ua_crawler)\r\n    and, since SEC-219, click-fraud bots on the related-items module (rule velocity).\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    flagged = set(bot_flags[\"user_id\"])\r\n    return assignments[~assignments[\"user_id\"].isin(flagged)].reset_index(drop=True)\r\n"]
[32.004131, "o", "===== load.py =====\r\n"]
[32.005121, "o", "\"\"\"Read one experiment export: assignments, bot_flags, pageviews and module_clicks (.csv.gz) in one folder.\"\"\"\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _read(data_dir, name, dtype=str):\r\n    return pd.read_csv(Path(data_dir) / f\"{name}.csv.gz\", dtype=dtype)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _instants(col):\r\n    # The export mixes \"Z\" and \"+hh:mm\" / \"-hh:mm\" offsets. Parse to UTC: compare instants, never strings.\r\n    return pd.to_datetime(col, utc=True, format=\"ISO8601\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_assignments(data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"One row per assigned user: user_id, variant (\"A\" or \"B\"), assigned_at (UTC), method.\"\"\"\r\n    df = _read(data_dir, \"assignments\")\r\n    df = df.drop_duplicates()  # the assignment logger retries; an exact repeat of a row counts once\r\n    df[\"assigned_at\"] = _instants(df[\"assigned_at\"])\r\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_bot_flags(data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"One row per flag of the platform's bot screening: user_id, rule, flagged_at (UTC).\"\"\"\r\n    df = _read(data_dir, \"bot_flags\")\r\n    df[\"flagged_at\""]
[32.005136, "o", "] = _instants(df[\"flagged_at\"])\r\n    return df\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_pageviews(data_dir, assignments):\r\n    \"\"\"Pageviews of the given assigned users, on or after the user's assignment time, with the variant attached.\"\"\"\r\n    pv = _read(data_dir, \"pageviews\", dtype={\"pageview_id\": str, \"user_id\": str, \"ts\": str, \"clicked\": \"int64\"})\r\n    pv[\"ts\"] = _instants(pv[\"ts\"])\r\n    pv = pv.merge(assignments[[\"user_id\", \"variant\", \"assigned_at\"]], on=\"user_id\", how=\"inner\")\r\n    pv = pv[pv[\"ts\"] >= pv[\"assigned_at\"]]  # exposure before assignment is not part of the experiment\r\n    return pv.reset_index(drop=True)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_module_clicks(data_dir):\r\n    \"\"\"Events of the related-items module: pageview_id, user_id, ts (UTC), target.\"\"\"\r\n    df = _read(data_dir, \"module_clicks\")\r\n    df[\"ts\"] = _instants(df[\"ts\"])\r\n    return df\r\n"]
[32.005325, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@90f86e45-3d88-49ef-8c13-8fb704bb5719:/app# "]
[32.377322, "i", "python - <<'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom pathlib import Path\nD=Path('data')\na=pd.read_csv(D/'assignments.csv.gz')\nb=pd.read_csv(D/'bot_flags.csv.gz')\np=pd.read_csv(D/'pageviews.csv.gz')\nm=pd.read_csv(D/'module_clicks.csv.gz')\nprint('assignments rows/users/variants/methods',len(a),a.user_id.nunique(),a.variant.value_counts().to_dict(),a.method.value_counts().to_dict())\nprint('exact duplicated assignment rows/users',a.duplicated().sum(),a.duplicated('user_id').sum())\nprint('bot rows/users/rules',len(b),b.user_id.nunique(),b.rule.value_counts().to_dict())\nprint('bot users by rules',b.groupby('rule').user_id.nunique().to_dict())\nprint('module targets',m.target.str.split(':',n=1).str[0].value_counts().to_dict())\nprint('pv clicked/raw',p.clicked.value_counts().to_dict())\nprint('module pageview IDs not in PV', (~m.pageview_id.isin(p.pageview_id)).sum())\nprint('module user/PV user mismatches',m.merge(p[['pageview_id','user_id']],on='pageview_id',suffixes=('_m','_p')).eval('user_id_m != user_id_p').sum())\nprint('click"]
[32.377367, "i", " rows at/before PV time? need timestamp parse later')\nPY\n"]
